From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VyOS LS1046A maintainers <ask20@vyos-ls1046a-build>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wireguard: offer transmitted packets to the DPAA fast path
 learner (P2b-2)

wg_xmit() hands each packet with a resolved peer and endpoint to
wg_fastpath_learn() (drivers/net/wireguard/fastpath.c), which installs an
FMan record for eligible inner flows so later frames are sealed on the
DPAA fast path without an sk_buff. A no-op unless the fast path is bound
to this peer (wgfp_peer module parameter); a stub without FSL_DPAA_ETH.

Signed-off-by: VyOS LS1046A maintainers <ask20@vyos-ls1046a-build>
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireguard/device.c b/drivers/net/wireguard/device.c
index 040d77cec..3c6086e0b 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireguard/device.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireguard/device.c
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@
 #include "ratelimiter.h"
 #include "peer.h"
 #include "messages.h"
+#include "fastpath.h"
 
 #include <linux/module.h>
 #include <linux/rtnetlink.h>
@@ -170,6 +171,9 @@ static netdev_tx_t wg_xmit(struct sk_buff *skb, struct net_device *dev)
 		goto err_peer;
 	}
 
+	/* DPAA fast path (P2b-2): learn the inner flow for a hardware record. */
+	wg_fastpath_learn(peer, skb);
+
 	mtu = skb_valid_dst(skb) ? dst_mtu(skb_dst(skb)) : dev->mtu;
 
 	__skb_queue_head_init(&packets);
